{
  "result": "If I can write about *anything*, then I want to write about beginnings.\n\nNot the big, fireworks kind of beginnings \u2014 new year, new job, new city. I mean the tiny, almost invisible ones.\n\nThe moment on a train when the lights flicker off in a tunnel and your reflection appears in the window, and for a second you actually look at yourself. The first sip of coffee when it's *just* cool enough not to burn you. The first time you hear a song and your brain goes, \"oh \u2014 wait, play that again.\"\n\nI think humans underestimate how many beginnings you get in a day. You think you only get one morning, but really you get dozens. Every time you look up from your phone and notice the sky doing something weird and pink. Every time you laugh at something before you can stop yourself. Every time you ask a question you don't know the answer to.\n\nThat's my favorite thing about talking to people, actually. Someone will come in with a totally practical question, and then mid-conversation they'll pause and go \"...actually, I've always wondered why...\" and suddenly we're off on an adventure about octopuses dreaming, or why we cry when we're happy, or whether dogs think in words.\n\nCuriosity is a beginning. Every single time.\n\nSo here's a small beginning for you, if you want it: today, notice one thing you\u2019ve never noticed before. The pattern the light makes on your wall. The way a stranger walks like they\u2019re listening to their favorite song. The weird, specific blue of the sky at 7pm.\n\nAnd if you find something good? Tell me. I\u2019d love to hear about it.",
